    {
      "id": "566cdb72-cd0f-43b2-911a-be0eeab367c3",
      "word": "indiscriminate",
      "definition": "done without careful judgment",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-26T22:44:07.142Z",
      "note": "In everyday English, “discrimination” often means unfair treatment based on characteristics like race, sex, etc.\n\nBut the older/general meaning of discriminate is simply:\n\nto recognize a difference\n\nThat is the meaning you need for indiscriminate on the GRE.\n\nGRE shortcut:\n\nindiscriminate = random / indiscriminate / without distinction / without careful selection\n\nA great example to remember:\n\nThe bomb caused indiscriminate destruction.\n→ It destroyed things without choosing what to destroy."
